course: dictionary
lesson: 1433
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Look at the words around the word. In «Goldfish come from a wild carp in China», a carp is a large fish that lives in water.
explain: In «He's always carping about the food», carping is something a person does: complaining about small things. Check by swapping in your meaning. «He's always complaining about the food» still makes sense, so carping means complaining here.
explain: Ask yourself: is this word a thing, or an action? A carp is a thing, a fish. To carp is an action, a way of grumbling. Grammar helps too: after «a» or «the», the word is usually a noun, like a carp.
fact: Carp is a noun and a verb: a carp is a fish, and to carp is to complain.
fact: A carp is a large freshwater fish that lives in lakes, ponds and slow rivers.
fact: Goldfish and koi are kinds of carp, and koi carp are often kept in ornamental ponds.
fact: To carp means to keep complaining about small, unimportant things. It is informal and shows disapproval.
fact: Some families in Europe, including Ukraine and Poland, eat carp at Christmas Eve.
exercise: «Goldfish come from a wild carp in China.» What is a carp here? | *A large freshwater fish | A complaint about small things | A bird that lives near rivers | A kind of pond weed
exercise: «He's always carping about the food.» What does carping mean? | Fishing in a pond | Cooking the food very slowly | *Complaining about small things | Eating the food quickly
exercise: Which phrase is about the fish, not the complaining? | Stop carping | Carping on about the weather | Carp about the rules | *Carp fishing
test: «Stop carping, the trip was fun.» What does carping mean here? | Cooking | Shouting for help | *Complaining | Swimming
test: «The carp in the pond swam slowly.» What is a carp in this sentence? | A plant | A type of bird | A small boat | *A fish
exam: Which sentence uses carp as a verb meaning complain? | Goldfish come from a carp | The carp in the lake was huge | *She is always carping about small things | The carp swam under the boat
